MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B01_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B01_m01_001: The Divine Sovereign told me you'd be coming.\nPlease, go on inside.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B01_m01: <BLN>Queen Theodora of Saramis, yes?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01_001: No words can express my apologies for allowing this\nto happen in Your Majesty's absence.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01_002: I will do all in my power to bring this crisis to\na swift resolution.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01_003: We should hold a war council and {SetColor=Gold}go to battle{SetColor=Default} at\nonce. Do I have your leave, Your Majesty?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01_004: <ICA>Say yes.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01_005: <ICB>Say no.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Kon_m01: <BLN>No apology will suffice.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01_001: All our information indicates that Prince Dyan is\nin league with the Mosa.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01_006: Yet I can still scarcely believe he would go so far as\nto conspire with our enemies to threaten his home.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01_002: Even if the scheme succeeds, he will never have the\nsupport of the people afterward.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01_003: As foolish as it sounds...I suspect his deeper goal is\nto provoke Your Majesty.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01_004: In these circumstances, it is most fortunate that\nAurora suppressed the malice in your arm.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Bon_m01: <BLN>There is at least one silver lining.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01_001: I can't get over that kid Cai being Aurora's boy!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01_002: I knew there was something different about him,\nand now I finally get why.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01_003: Y'know, when I think about that little incident we\nhad right after coming to Dagsion...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01_004: It might've been the first link in a chain that led\nyou all the way here, boss.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01_005: Life's a funny thing, ain't it?
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Tob_m01: <BLN>You never can tell what'll happen.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_001: Hey, uh, Your Majesty...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_002: I'm sorry we couldn't stay to finish out the Heroic\nGames. You were so close to winning.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_003: <NCA>Agree.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_004: <NCB>Ask her true intentions.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_005: <ACA>Yeah... Just one more win and we'd have come out\non top.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_006: <ACA>I'm still annoyed that the Mosa chose now of all\ntimes to make their move.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_007: <ACB>Oh, uh...don't worry, Your Majesty. I'm all the way\non your side.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_008: <ACB>Plus, I seriously wanted to help you achieve what you\nwanted to do.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_009: <ACB>If only just to see your face when you made\nit happen.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01_010: <ACB>I mean, what would it look like for you to be truly\nhappy? Would it be weirdly cute, or what?
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lil_m01: <BLN>It's a real shame.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01_001: It seems that the people of Dagsion are not yet\naware of the goings-on in Saramis.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01_002: Even so, gossip travels fast. Once the news arrives,\nit will be widely known.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01_004: I hope this misstep does not lead to increased\ncriticism of our homeland.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01_005: We must aim to recapture Fort Zanbar as soon as\npossible to quell the uprising.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lys_m01: <BLN>We must aim for a swift resolution.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tro_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tro_m01_001: So that's what was happening in Saramis... I see.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tro_m01_003: I can't go with you to help right now, but I can at\nleast wish you luck.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tro_m01_004: The fate of Saramis depends on you. What you\nchoose to do next will shape your future.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Tro_m01: <BLN>I wish you luck.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02_001: This is my first time setting foot in the dead city\nof Ahm Lu.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02_002: I grant that it has been over five hundred years since\nthe fall of Damascar.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02_003: Yet almost nothing of its original splendor remains...\nA terrible pity.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02_004: Was Dagda the Great really so frightened of\nour ancestors?
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Bon_m02: <BLN>A terrible pity...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m02_001: I dunno what to say. The whole place was left to rot\nafter the slaughter here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m02_002: Weird that there's no animals or anything, when the\nplants seem to be doin' fine.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m02_003: For a whole country to be destroyed all at once...\nI don't like it, boss.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Tob_m02: <BLN>I don't like it.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02_001: Yeah, this is too much for me. I've been on edge ever\nsince we got here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02_002: It's like I sense someone nearby...like that feeling of\nsomeone watching you.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02_003: I don't know how else to put it. It's giving me the\nshakes, though.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02_004: Queen Theodora, can we hurry up and get out\nof here?
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lil_m02: <BLN>This place is too much for me...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02_001: If I recall, it was year 881 on the Imperial Calendar\nwhen the imperial army invaded this city.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02_002: The Cleansing of Damascar is a terrible memory for\nus—for all the forest peoples.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02_003: Yet rather than put it out of our minds, we must\ncontinue to tell the story, ghastly as it is.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02_004: I can still clearly remember my parents relating it\nto me when I was small.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lys_m02: <BLN>We must remember this tragedy.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m03_001: It is a strange coincidence that we should return to\nMegaira via this route.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m03_002: However, if we can quell this situation, our wish will\nbe heard as if we had won the Heroic Games.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Bon_m03_003: Even securing a verbal agreement from the Divine\nSovereign was a significant step toward our goal.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Bon_m03: <BLN>What an unusual coincidence.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03_001: Prince Dyan's nothing but trouble these days.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03_002: I liked him better as a kid, when he was cuter and\nplayed nice with you, boss.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03_003: But I guess this won't be over until you take off his\nhead yourself.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03_004: Why couldn't he have just stood by you like\nfamily should?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03_005: Even if you have different mothers, King Sergio's\nblood is in both of you.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Tob_m03: <BLN>That guy's nothing but trouble...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03_001: I was able to catch up with an old family friend\njust now.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03_002: Good news—my dad wasn't part of the uprising.\nSo that's a relief.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03_003: Probably just because Prince Dyan didn't reach out\nto him...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03_004: If he had, my dad definitely would've signed on.\nI bet he's even disappointed.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lil_m03: <BLN>What a relief...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03_001: Fort Zanbar is the key to defending Saramis from\nSouthern Dagda.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03_002: It's fair to say that the future of our country depends\non our victory.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03_003: I'll admit, I can't contain my excitement in the face\nof such a pivotal battle.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03_004: If I don't rein it in, I may end up doing\nsomething rash.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Lys_m03: <BLN>This is far too exciting.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Hoo_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Hoo_m01_001: Your Majesty, I will fight at your side in this battle.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Hoo_m01_002: I know my part in the prior conflict between Your\nMajesty and Prince Dyan casts me in a poor light.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_Hoo_m01_003: But I will be Your Majesty's loyal retainer until the\nend, even if some would think me a traitor for it.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_Hoo_m01: <BLN>I will be loyal to the end.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B02_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B02_m01_001: I'm so sorry about the Heroic Games,\nQueen Theodora.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B02_m01_002: But I think we would all rather have you back here.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B02_m01_003: Now that you've returned, Saramis cannot lose!
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B02_m01: <BLN>We're happy to have you back.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B03_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B03_m01_001: Fort Zanbar is an old stronghold originally controlled\nby the Mosa.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B03_m01_002: Saramis captured it during the War of Grania and\nwent to some trouble to heavily fortify it.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B03_m01_003: Ever since, it's been the linchpin of our defense\nagainst the Mosa. I regret to see them retake it.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B03_m01: <BLN>How regrettable.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B04_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B04_m01_001: Welcome back, Queen Theodora! I'm glad to see\nyou're still OK.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B04_m01_002: Are the bad guys gonna invade here if Grania\nStronghold gets taken over?
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B04_m01_003: Well, I won't let them! I'm gonna get a sword and\nshield and fight for you too!
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B04_m01: <BLN>I'll fight too!
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B05_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B05_m01_001: Everything was in turmoil for a while there, but\nwe've got a grasp on what happened now.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B05_m01_002: It seems the Mosa killed a messenger traveling to\nand from Fort Zanbar and replaced them.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B05_m01_003: Then they spread misinformation in Fort Zanbar and\ndeployed Mosa forces near the Kurdelind Ruins.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B05_m01_004: While we were busy there, they invaded through\na hidden passage and seized the fort at a stroke.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B05_m01: <BLN>We know what happened now.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01_001: I was stationed at Fort Zanbar when it happened.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01_002: We got word that the Mosa had launched a sudden\nattack on Megaira from the sea.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01_003: Half the troops from Fort Zanbar were dispatched\nto Megaira in a rush to send aid.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01_004: I was one of them. While we were on our way to the\npalace, we got word that the fort had been overrun.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B06_m01_005: There was no way to know anymore what was true\nand what was a lie.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B06_m01: <BLN>They fooled us completely...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B07_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B07_m01_001: Our findings leave no room for doubt that the Mosa\nand Prince Dyan are working together.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B07_m01_002: We think soldiers and officers from Dyan's faction\nhad already infiltrated Fort Zanbar.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B07_m01_003: With a large part of its forces elsewhere, Fort Zanbar\nwas seized through practically no effort.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B07_m01_004: I never knew that Prince Dyan still had so many\nsupporters...
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B07_m01: <BLN>It came as a shock.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01_001: He may have done it through trickery, but I'm still\nimpressed he took THE Fort Zanbar.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01_002: I have to say, his idea to coordinate with the Mosa\nwas a brilliant tactic.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01_003: Maybe Prince Dyan does have some talent as a\ngeneral after all...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01_004: Which makes it all such a pity he didn't use his guile\nto support Your Majesty.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B08_m01_005: The future of Saramis could've been even brighter...
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B08_m01: <BLN>It's such a pity...
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B09_m01: <TH>
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B09_m01_001: Queen Theodora! I'll be among your troops for the\nupcoming battle.
MID_LGV_1SEO_c12_B09_m01_002: Fighting on the same battlefield as Your Majesty\nis an honor I'll tell my grandchildren about.
MID_LGA_1SEO_c12_B09_m01: <BLN>I'm ready to serve you!